<p style="font-size:0.85rem;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:12px">League: exactly 20-minute slots, with two 10-minute sets. Use a shared external clock for both courts and switch sides immediately. Finish the rally at each buzzer; if a set is tied, play one deciding rally. Start set 2 at 0–0. No tactical timeouts. Winning both sets earns 2 league points; 1–1 is a draw worth 1 point each; losing both earns 0. Rank by league points, point difference, points scored, then team registration order. Court 1: semifinal 1 (1st vs 4th), semifinal 2 (2nd vs 3rd), then the final. These matches are first to win two sets; the deciding third set is to 15. Court 2: places 5–7 play a fresh round robin, first to win two sets per match, with a deciding third set to 15. Placement matches cannot end in a draw. The first two sets are to 25. All point-based sets require a two-point lead.</p>
